            <ArticleTitle>Complete occlusion of the left main coronary artery: successful surgical management by myocardial revascularization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1118-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated total occlusion of the left main coronary artery was demonstrated on coronary cineangiography in a 50-year-old woman with a progressive anginal syndrome. Aortocoronary saphenous vein graft bypass was performed. Six weeks after operation the patient was free of symptoms and postoperative coronary angiography showed the graft to be patent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
